## Story Description
Create data/reference/savings_rates.yaml containing per-lever savings rates and addressability percentages. The file has two top-level keys: 'defaults' (one entry per lever type as fallback) and 'categories' (L1 category overrides). Each entry has saving_pct (float 0-1) and addressability_pct (float 0-1). Lever type keys must exactly match the constants in src/recommendations/rules.py: SUPPLIER_CONSOLIDATION, PAYMENT_TERM_EXTENSION, TAIL_SPEND_RATIONALISATION, CONTRACT_COMPLIANCE, COMPETITIVE_TENDER, CONTRACT_COVERAGE_GAP. Default values: SUPPLIER_CONSOLIDATION saving_pct=0.08 addressability_pct=0.70; COMPETITIVE_TENDER saving_pct=0.07 addressability_pct=0.65; CONTRACT_COVERAGE_GAP saving_pct=0.05 addressability_pct=0.80; TAIL_SPEND_RATIONALISATION saving_pct=0.10 addressability_pct=0.50; CONTRACT_COMPLIANCE saving_pct=0.05 addressability_pct=0.75; PAYMENT_TERM_EXTENSION has no saving_pct (uses WACC formula) so omit saving_pct and set addressability_pct=0.80. Category overrides for: 'Information Technology' (SUPPLIER_CONSOLIDATION: saving_pct=0.12 addressability_pct=0.65; COMPETITIVE_TENDER: saving_pct=0.10 addressability_pct=0.60), 'Professional Services' (SUPPLIER_CONSOLIDATION: saving_pct=0.10 addressability_pct=0.55; COMPETITIVE_TENDER: saving_pct=0.08 addressability_pct=0.50), 'Facilities Management' (SUPPLIER_CONSOLIDATION: saving_pct=0.07 addressability_pct=0.72), 'Marketing and Communications' (SUPPLIER_CONSOLIDATION: saving_pct=0.12 addressability_pct=0.60), 'Logistics and Transport' (COMPETITIVE_TENDER: saving_pct=0.09 addressability_pct=0.70).

## Acceptance Criteria
- Create file: data/reference/savings_rates.yaml
- Verify: python3 -c "import yaml; d=yaml.safe_load(open('data/reference/savings_rates.yaml')); print(list(d.keys()))" — prints ['defaults', 'categories'] without error
