## Story Description
Create src/recommendations/deduplicator.py containing a SpendAllocator class that prevents two recommendations from double-counting the same spend pool. EXCLUSIVE_GROUPS mapping at module level: {'SUPPLIER_CONSOLIDATION': 'SOURCING', 'COMPETITIVE_TENDER': 'SOURCING', 'CONTRACT_COVERAGE_GAP': 'COVERAGE', 'PAYMENT_TERM_EXTENSION': 'WORKING_CAPITAL', 'TAIL_SPEND_RATIONALISATION': 'PORTFOLIO_TAIL', 'CONTRACT_COMPLIANCE': 'PORTFOLIO_COMPLIANCE'}. SpendAllocator.allocate(recommendations: list[dict]) -> list[dict]: (1) Sort input by estimated_impact_aud descending. (2) For each rec, compute pool_key: for PORTFOLIO_* groups use ('PORTFOLIO', exclusive_group); for all others use (rec['context'], exclusive_group). (3) If pool_key is already in claimed set: set rec['estimated_impact_aud'] = 0.0, set rec['deduplication_note'] = 'Spend pool already claimed by higher-impact recommendation of same exclusive group'. (4) Else: add pool_key to claimed set. (5) After processing all recs, filter out those where estimated_impact_aud == 0.0. (6) Return filtered list. Work on a deep copy of the input list to avoid mutating callers' data.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Create file: src/recommendations/deduplicator.py
- Run: python3 -m py_compile src/recommendations/deduplicator.py — succeeds
- Verify: python3 -c "from src.recommendations.deduplicator import SpendAllocator; recs=[{'type':'SUPPLIER_CONSOLIDATION','context':'IT Services','estimated_impact_aud':100.0,'lever':'x'},{'type':'COMPETITIVE_TENDER','context':'IT Services','estimated_impact_aud':80.0,'lever':'x'}]; out=SpendAllocator().allocate(recs); print(len(out))" — prints 1 (only higher-impact survives)
- Verify: python3 -c "from src.recommendations.deduplicator import SpendAllocator; recs=[{'type':'SUPPLIER_CONSOLIDATION','context':'IT Services','estimated_impact_aud':100.0,'lever':'x'},{'type':'CONTRACT_COVERAGE_GAP','context':'IT Services','estimated_impact_aud':80.0,'lever':'x'}]; out=SpendAllocator().allocate(recs); print(len(out))" — prints 2 (different groups, both kept)

